Black Box OS: open-source code
Copyright notices and licences

Black Box OS is distributed by Angry Owl Labs LLC. It is built from Debian GNU/Linux (trixie), Arduino's Debian image
for the Arduino UNO Q (base image 20260528-558) and Arduino's Linux kernel for the UNO Q, plus a few Linux kernel
drivers that we build, unmodified, from that same kernel source, and Dashivo's own software.

This repository holds the source code, or the exact location and checksum of the source code, of the open-source
software in each Black Box OS release, and the scripts we use to build the kernel modules we add.

Every component keeps its own licence and its own copyright notices:

  - The Linux kernel and the kernel modules we build: GPL-2.0 (with the Linux-syscall-note), some files dual-licensed
    (for example GPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause for rtw88 / rtw89, BSD-3-Clause-Clear for mt76).
    See LICENSES/Linux-kernel-COPYING.txt and the LICENSES folder inside the kernel source archive.
  - Debian packages: each under the licences named in its debian/copyright file, which is part of the package's
    source and is also installed on the device at /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright. releases/<version>/packages.tsv
    lists the licences of every package of that release.
  - Arduino's packages (arduino-cli, arduino-router, arduino-app-lab, arduino-linux-config): GPL-3.0, with the
    third-party notices in their own copyright files.
  - Qualcomm's rebuild of PipeWire (LGPL-2.1+ and MIT): Debian's source plus Qualcomm's published change.

